  "solution": {
    "text": "The orbitals which belongs to same subshell&nbsp;and same shell are called degenerate orbitals.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext>3d</mtext><mtext>xy</mtext></msub><msub><mtext>,&nbsp;3d</mtext><msup><mtext>z</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><msub><mtext>,&nbsp;3d</mtext><mtext>yz</mtext></msub></mrow></mfenced><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext>4d</mtext><mtext>xy</mtext></msub><msub><mtext>,&nbsp;4d</mtext><mtext>yz</mtext></msub><msub><mtext>,&nbsp;4d</mtext><msup><mtext>z</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> are the two sets of degenerate orbitals."
